  "coverage_limits": [
    "The reconstruction is restricted to the complete supplied material concerning Supreme Court Civil Appeal No. 497 of 1957, decided May 4, 1961, and the registered identification questions relating to plot No. 1060.",
    "All documentary contents, historical circumstances and judicial findings are recorded as reported by the target judgment. The original final decree, sale certificate, delivery writ, sale deed and cadastral records have not been independently authenticated.",
    "The statuses distinguish the parties' arguments, reported documentary descriptions, Patna High Court findings and the Supreme Court's own assessments. TRUE denotes support for the specifically attributed proposition, not automatic proof of any allegation embedded within it.",
    "The literal appearance of plot number 160 and the judicial identification of plot 1060 are preserved as separate propositions. The recorded designation 160 must not be treated as proof that a separate plot 160 existed in khata 97.",
    "The judicial-sale transaction and the subsequent conveyance to the respondents remain distinct. References to the respondents' predecessors-in-interest do not independently establish additional identities or transactions beyond the supplied account.",
    "The decisive identification particulars are the corresponding khata number, area and boundaries, the additional documentary references to 1060, and the absence of plot 160 in khata 97. Their original measurements and descriptions are not reproduced in the supplied source.",
